#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""promoter-bot (formerly churn): stateless driver for GitGalaxy's continuous churn (the night-shift skill).

The expensive part of the old churn was one long orchestrator session re-reading its
whole context on every tick. Here nothing stays alive:

  churn tick                 run by a systemd user timer. Cheap checks first (stop file,
                             pause, finished workers, PR changes, a launch slot); a
                             headless `claude -p "/night-shift tick"` runs ONLY when one of
                             them needs judgment. Opus when a worker report waits for review,
                             Sonnet otherwise. Quiet ticks cost no model tokens.
  churn worker ...           start one detached headless worker in its own worktree. Its
                             JSON result (report, cost, session id, permission denials) lands
                             in $H/churn-runs/<run>/ and the next tick reaps it.
  churn send-back RUN MSG    resume that worker's own session with a fix request.
  churn agy ...              start one detached agy (Antigravity/Gemini) worker: separate quota, separate
                             pause, no Claude tokens. Its result is checked by a Sonnet checker that the
                             gate launches by itself, before the normal review.
  churn status               what is running, pending, spent; timer state.
  churn worktrees            remove finished worktrees now (the gate does it every 6 h); --dry-run lists.
  churn notify test|status   phone alerts via ntfy (topic in $H/churn-notify.json); `churn watchdog` runs hourly.
  churn claims               this host's issue claims (`claim:<host_id>` labels; other hosts and people skip them).

All state stays in $H/churn-state.json (shared with the night-shift skill).
"""

